# Kima Compliance Quality Gate

Before implementing a significant feature:
- Identify the business problem and requirement being addressed.
- Define acceptance criteria and expected user behavior.
- Identify affected frontend, backend and database components.

After implementing a significant feature:
- Request independent verification using kima-qa-auditor.
- Use available ECC technical reviewers for specialized checks.
- Confirm frontend/backend behavior and role permissions.
- Run relevant tests and identify any untested behavior.
- Record deviations from approved requirements.

Do not call a feature complete based only on successful
code generation, compilation, or visual appearance.

Do not claim release readiness when P0 or P1 defects
remain unresolved.

Do not implement suggested fixes without authorization.
